00:00:12.220 --> 00:00:14.530
MARKUS KLUTE: Welcome
back to 8.701.

00:00:14.530 --> 00:00:16.720
So in this second chapter--

00:00:16.720 --> 00:00:19.300
chapter number 1-- we
start talking about

00:00:19.300 --> 00:00:22.180
quarks' and leptons'
interactions and fields.

00:00:22.180 --> 00:00:24.460
And we start by a very
general discussion

00:00:24.460 --> 00:00:26.560
of quantum fields and matter.

00:00:26.560 --> 00:00:30.400
So you all know what we
mean by particles and forces

00:00:30.400 --> 00:00:32.720
in the classical sense.

00:00:32.720 --> 00:00:36.640
However, we need now to see
how they connect with quantum

00:00:36.640 --> 00:00:40.840
fields, and how this helps us
to consider matter and forces

00:00:40.840 --> 00:00:42.080
in a very similar way.

00:00:45.710 --> 00:00:51.230
The modern view of the basic
way that particles come to exist

00:00:51.230 --> 00:00:54.590
is in terms of
quantized fields, which

00:00:54.590 --> 00:00:59.600
is an extension of the quantum
mechanics you love and know,

00:00:59.600 --> 00:01:03.860
which you have done before,
where you quantize particles.

00:01:03.860 --> 00:01:07.640
These fields have quantum
equations for their field

00:01:07.640 --> 00:01:11.510
amplitudes which are
basically like the quantum

00:01:11.510 --> 00:01:14.630
simple harmonic
oscillator, but there are

00:01:14.630 --> 00:01:16.590
an infinite number of them--

00:01:16.590 --> 00:01:21.000
one for every possible
frequency of wave in the field.

00:01:21.000 --> 00:01:25.760
This means the amplitudes for
the wave for each frequency

00:01:25.760 --> 00:01:30.330
are therefore quantized
in integer steps,

00:01:30.330 --> 00:01:33.060
just like in a simple
harmonic oscillator.

00:01:33.060 --> 00:01:36.510
This is what we
see as a particle.

00:01:36.510 --> 00:01:40.400
The first excitation gives
one particle of a frequency.

00:01:40.400 --> 00:01:43.740
The further excitation
of the amplitude

00:01:43.740 --> 00:01:47.600
for the same frequency
corresponds to two particles.

00:01:47.600 --> 00:01:49.220
Et cetera, et cetera.

00:01:49.220 --> 00:01:51.530
So hence, the concept
of quantum field,

00:01:51.530 --> 00:01:53.510
unlike normal quantum
mechanics, allows

00:01:53.510 --> 00:01:58.220
an arbitrary and changeable
number of particles to exist.

00:01:58.220 --> 00:02:02.090
This is necessary, as
you will see later,

00:02:02.090 --> 00:02:05.810
such that we can create
and annihilate particles

00:02:05.810 --> 00:02:09.229
in reactions and decays.

00:02:09.229 --> 00:02:11.030
And the standard
wavefunctions correspond

00:02:11.030 --> 00:02:13.520
to an equation of a
particular frequency,

00:02:13.520 --> 00:02:17.331
amplitude when it exists
in the [INAUDIBLE]..

00:02:20.280 --> 00:02:25.280
So now, just let's
consider a few cases here.

00:02:25.280 --> 00:02:28.790
Imagine you have two particles--
two fermions, for example--

00:02:28.790 --> 00:02:30.980
let's say two electrons.

00:02:30.980 --> 00:02:33.500
And you consider
the wavefunction.

00:02:33.500 --> 00:02:35.690
Quantum field
theory actually says

00:02:35.690 --> 00:02:38.270
that there's only
one electron quantum

00:02:38.270 --> 00:02:41.910
field for the whole universe,
and every electron which exists

00:02:41.910 --> 00:02:44.820
is due to an excitation
of the field.

00:02:44.820 --> 00:02:46.590
Hence, all electrons
are identical

00:02:46.590 --> 00:02:49.020
in the quantum-mechanical
sense, as they all

00:02:49.020 --> 00:02:51.950
arise from the same field.

00:02:51.950 --> 00:02:55.920
The theory says, then, that
particular properties are

00:02:55.920 --> 00:02:58.740
the resulting wave equations--
namely, their symmetry--

00:02:58.740 --> 00:03:02.910
and the exchange
of these particles.

00:03:02.910 --> 00:03:06.740
So the extra symmetry
depends on whether or not

00:03:06.740 --> 00:03:10.520
the particle is a fermion,
which means it has spin 1/2

00:03:10.520 --> 00:03:16.700
or 3/2 or 5/2, et cetera, or a
boson, which means that it has

00:03:16.700 --> 00:03:20.190
spin 0, 1, or 2, and so on.

00:03:20.190 --> 00:03:23.570
So for any identical
fermion and electron,

00:03:23.570 --> 00:03:26.360
our quantum field theory
says that their wavefunction

00:03:26.360 --> 00:03:31.590
must obey the property
of antisymmetry.

00:03:31.590 --> 00:03:34.530
This means that when we
write an overall wavefunction

00:03:34.530 --> 00:03:39.360
and we replace the particles,
we pick up a minus sign.

00:03:39.360 --> 00:03:42.470
This property is not
just for electrons,

00:03:42.470 --> 00:03:44.540
but for all fermions--

00:03:44.540 --> 00:03:48.260
that's all matter particle,
as we saw last week.

00:03:48.260 --> 00:03:50.450
So it also holds for
composite particles.

00:03:50.450 --> 00:03:55.790
A composite spin-1/2 particle
is subject to the same

00:03:55.790 --> 00:03:56.600
antisymmetry.

00:03:59.250 --> 00:04:02.850
This property of exchange
antisymmetry leads

00:04:02.850 --> 00:04:09.420
to a well-known principle--
namely, the Pauli principle,

00:04:09.420 --> 00:04:12.540
which means that you cannot
have two electrons of the same

00:04:12.540 --> 00:04:17.130
energy state or the same state,
because when you would actually

00:04:17.130 --> 00:04:22.810
swap them, you find
that they are identical,

00:04:22.810 --> 00:04:25.930
which is a stark contrast to
the actual description of this

00:04:25.930 --> 00:04:26.790
wavefunction.

00:04:26.790 --> 00:04:27.990
So this doesn't really work.

00:04:27.990 --> 00:04:30.210
And therefore, two
electrons, or two fermions,

00:04:30.210 --> 00:04:33.420
cannot be in the same state.

00:04:33.420 --> 00:04:34.770
[INAUDIBLE] very general.

00:04:34.770 --> 00:04:39.840
Constructing a wavefunction or
a total wave equation for two

00:04:39.840 --> 00:04:41.386
fermions is not that hard.

00:04:41.386 --> 00:04:46.560
We can simply do this
by this construction.

00:04:49.850 --> 00:04:53.840
An important additional
statement or note to take here

00:04:53.840 --> 00:04:57.020
is that an antiparticle
such as a positron

00:04:57.020 --> 00:05:03.380
is not identical to a particle,
such as to the electron, again.

00:05:03.380 --> 00:05:07.430
If you move on to bosons,
boson exchange is symmetric,

00:05:07.430 --> 00:05:09.890
meaning that if you
[? request ?] two photons,

00:05:09.890 --> 00:05:12.140
you find the identical
wavefunction.

00:05:12.140 --> 00:05:16.500
And then constructing a
two-boson total wavefunction,

00:05:16.500 --> 00:05:19.550
you do this by adding those
two functions together.

00:05:19.550 --> 00:05:24.330
This is, by
definition, symmetric.

00:05:24.330 --> 00:05:27.350
Let's look now forward
to exchange particles.

00:05:27.350 --> 00:05:30.495
Again, you have a very good
idea of the classical picture

00:05:30.495 --> 00:05:33.620
of how forces are transmitted.

00:05:33.620 --> 00:05:40.190
So the modern picture of how a
force acts under quantization

00:05:40.190 --> 00:05:43.580
is by emission and by
absorption of a particle.

00:05:43.580 --> 00:05:45.950
That is shown in
this diagram here,

00:05:45.950 --> 00:05:49.490
where let's say you have an
electron and a second electron.

00:05:49.490 --> 00:05:50.480
They see each other.

00:05:50.480 --> 00:05:54.920
And they see each other by
emitting and absorbing photons.

00:05:54.920 --> 00:05:56.005
And you see this here.

00:05:56.005 --> 00:05:59.880
So this electron comes along,
maybe emitting a photon.

00:05:59.880 --> 00:06:01.720
This electron [? readmits ?] it.

00:06:01.720 --> 00:06:05.100
And by this exchange of
emission and absorption

00:06:05.100 --> 00:06:08.630
of photon, those two
particles, the [INAUDIBLE]

00:06:08.630 --> 00:06:10.370
electrons to each other.

00:06:10.370 --> 00:06:14.660
So this you can think about
like two ships shooting cannons,

00:06:14.660 --> 00:06:15.230
if you want.

00:06:18.350 --> 00:06:20.810
But you also have to consider
that there is not just

00:06:20.810 --> 00:06:24.120
repelling forces, but
also attracting forces.

00:06:24.120 --> 00:06:27.050
We could have replaced the
electron with a positron,

00:06:27.050 --> 00:06:30.170
and the negative and
the positive charge

00:06:30.170 --> 00:06:33.660
would interact with each other.

00:06:33.660 --> 00:06:36.550
This is it for this short--

00:06:39.075 --> 00:06:42.820
it's basically an intro
into the intro of the intro.

00:06:42.820 --> 00:06:44.440
I hope you enjoy this.

00:06:44.440 --> 00:06:47.260
All of those concept
we go into more detail.

00:06:47.260 --> 00:06:49.605
This is really just
the starting point.

00:06:49.605 --> 00:06:50.980
And then the next
lecture, you'll

00:06:50.980 --> 00:06:54.820
see how we can
actually understand

00:06:54.820 --> 00:06:57.790
aspects of this
diagram here, which

00:06:57.790 --> 00:07:00.250
we call the Feynman diagram.

